# My everyday loaf based on morph

starter:
  ap_flour
  water
  hydration = 100%

leaven:
  starter
  bread_flour = 5 * starter
  cold_water
  extra = -20g
  hydration = 100%

grain:
  prairie_gold
  hard_red
  barley = 5%
  spelt = 5%
  buckwheat = 5%

dry:
  grain
  vwg = 3%
  potato_flakes = 5%
  flaxseed_meal = 5%
  yeast = 0.5%
  salt = 1.8%

wet:
  cold_water
  old_dough = 100g
  ascorbic_acid_1p = 50ppm * 100 * grain
  leaven = 40%
  olive_oil = 5%
  honey = 5%
  yogurt = 5%

dough:
  wet
  dry
  hydration = 70%
  old_dough = 0 - wet.old_dough # forgot to remove it
  total_flour = 500g # 9 inch

/*
August 16, 2026

Changes
- Using leaven I mixed this morning

Starter is 4 days old.

Mixed the leaven about 7:30 and into the proofer at 86F.

Started on dough at 13:30.

Leaven pH = 3.70 at 13:55 dt is 78F. It rose to the top of the 500ml
container and had started to fall.

# Dry T=84. Wet T=62. 

Used the KA for mixing. Mixed about 14:05. Stopped after 2 minutes;
it cleaned the bowl. DT after mixing is ?. RT is 78F. 

long rest in fridge during a thunderstorm.

Kneaded 10 minutes in KA. It was cleaning the bowl and looking great.

Into the cambro and onto the counter at 15:30.

Into the pan at 16:30. Left on the counter at 77F.

Baked at 17:35 for 45 minutes at 350F lid off.

I added 100ml of water to the pan after preheating the oven.


*/

